Credits

The permission model of warden -- groups with a numeric level, named
permissions granted to groups, a per-group vehicle cap, the rank rule that an
action needs a higher level than its target -- follows the semantics of
CobaltEssentials, a server plugin for another BeamNG multiplayer platform,
released under the GNU General Public License version 3 by its authors
(https://github.com/prestonelam2003/CobaltEssentials). No source code of
CobaltEssentials is included in warden; the semantics were reimplemented for
NodeMP's API, identity model and storage.

The in-game panel (warden-ui) was designed and written from scratch. Its
predecessor for the other platform, CobaltEssentialsInterface, is not
published under a free licence, so nothing of it -- code, strings or layout
constants -- was used.
